{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.global_imq_zero_swing_when_slopes_equal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.global_imq_zero_swing_when_slopes_equal","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**The order-mismatch, stated structurally.** A single global `Im(q₀)=ε` feeds the\nsame magnitude to both anchors, so its *swing* is only the difference of the two\nslopes `(k_p − k_m)·ε`. Since `k` is anchor-invariant to the `22 ppb` `q_r`\ndifference (`k_p = k_m` in the exact-equality idealization), that swing is exactly\nzero — the residual real-part channel supplies it, and the probe measures that\nchannel at `6.6×10⁶` below the observed swing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.required_imq_opposite_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.required_imq_opposite_sign","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L117-L130","doc":"**Opposite-sign requirement (parity `fig8Trace_im_odd`).** With positive slope\n`k>0`, realizing the observed `S_p < 0 < S_m` forces `ε_p < 0 < ε_m`: the required\n`Im(q)` FLIPS SIGN between the anchors. The sign is set by *which lepton/baryon ratio\npins `q₀`* — a pinning choice with no independent predictor — which is precisely why\nthe per-anchor solve is a fit, not a substrate measurement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.peranchor_imq_fits_anything","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.peranchor_imq_fits_anything","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L107-L115","doc":"**THE FIT — per-anchor `Im(q)` fits ANY pair of residuals (unfalsifiable knob).**\nFor nonzero slope `k` and ANY targets `Sp, Sm`, there exist per-anchor imaginary\nparts `εp, εm` with `phaseResponse k εp = Sp`, `phaseResponse k εm = Sm` (namely\n`εp = Sp/k`, `εm = Sm/k`). Two free parameters fit two data points — the guardrail's\nunfalsifiability made precise: a per-anchor `Im(q)` is a fit, never a measurement of\none substrate `Im(q₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.global_imq_cannot_realize_swing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.global_imq_cannot_realize_swing","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L95-L105","doc":"**FALSIFIABLE TEST — a single global `Im(q₀)` cannot realize the swing.** Both\nanchors are two pins of the same `q₀`; in a *global* model they share the same\nimaginary part `ε`, hence the same phase input, hence the **same** response\n`phaseResponse k ε`. A single value cannot equal two distinct targets `S_p ≠ S_m`.\nThis is `QOU.QBeta.SRigidity.no_anchor_invariant_realizes_swing` for the `Im(q)`\nchannel: an anchor-invariant `Im(q₀)` is anchor-invariant DATA, and the quantitative\nprobe shows the residual `q_r`-difference channel is `6.6×10⁶` too weak. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse_hasDerivAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse_hasDerivAt","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**The slope is realized at every `ε` (measurement leg).** `dS/dε = k`, a fixed,\nanchor-invariant slope — so the model *measures* `Im(q₀)` with the same\nproportionality at both anchors (this is the \"good news\" of the reframe, and exactly\nwhy a single `Im(q₀)` cannot explain a *swing*: the proportionality does not change\nbetween the anchors). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse_odd","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L82-L85","doc":"**Odd in `ε`** — the merged parity `fig8Trace_im_odd` (`sign S = sign Im q`) at\nthe linear level: `S(−ε) = −S(ε)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse_real_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse_real_zero","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L77-L80","doc":"**Real substrate ⇒ no signal** (`ε=0`), recovering #4293's real-ray\n`nzImVolume_real_ray` in the linearized model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQAnchorCarrier.phaseResponse","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQAnchorCarrier.lean#L70-L75","doc":"**Linear phase-channel response** `S = k·ε` in the substrate imaginary part\n`ε = Im(q₀)`, with slope `k = (∂S/∂φ|₀)·(d arg u/dε|₀) = √3 r²/(q_r log q_r)` (probe:\n`k = 0.651275` at the substrate). This is the leading form of the #4293 `nzImVolume`\nunder the `arg(u) ↔ Im(q₀)` linearization; nonlinear corrections do not rescue the\nverdict (probe carries the exact, non-linearized comparison). ","signatureChunk":0}]}